WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.380
What's up, everybody. Jared again

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.469
Today we're talking about anime's most powerful pipsqueak

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.120
Sorry about that, Edward.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.700
Now, "Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood" has all the trappings of an instant classic

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.520
High concept science fiction.....

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.680
Check!

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.320
Awesome fight scenes..

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:23.820
Definitely!

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.700
Strong philosophical core?

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.660
Well, that's why we're here!

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.860
Throughout Edward and Alphonse's journey to restore their bodies,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.160
the two are confronted with various discourses on the efficacy and

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.980
application of science or in their case "Alchemy".

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.730
Sure it's through alchemy that they hope to recover their bodies

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.960
But they also see it used for some pretty awful things

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.320
So what is "Brotherhood" saying about Science

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.260
and the way it's applied to this world?

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.900
And how does faith fit into this discussion?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.680
Well, let's find out.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.860
Welcome to this Wisecrack edition on the philosophy of "Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood".

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.136
And of course!

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:03.920
Spoilers Ahead!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.040
But first a quick primer

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.760
"Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood" is set in Amestris.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.640
A country reminiscent of pre-World War 2 Europe whose defining feature is the success of

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.929
Alchemy or the manipulation and altering of matter using natural energy

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.880
Alchemy is essentially treated as a science

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.860
one that combines chemistry and biology with its own unique laws and principles

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.260
Alchemy's most important law

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.040
"The Law of Equivalent Exchange"

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.740
Or you know the law that means if you get the right materials and draw a circle

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.720
You can do this!

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.360
The show establishes a push and pull dynamic between science and Faith almost immediately.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.180
In Episode 3 , Ed and Al travel to the desert town of Liore to investigate

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:55.860
Father Cornello, a holy figure who has gained control of the people by awe-ing them with Miracles and

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.600
Indoctrinating them in the faith of Leto-ism

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.600
The second they arrive though, the brothers make their views abundantly clear to the faithful.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.480
And their skepticism toward the divine is justified

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.600
And it turns out Cornello's miracles are just cleverly veiled

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.440
applications of Alchemy that he uses to attract followers willing to die for him.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.980
Ed in Al expose Cornello is a fraud and

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.260
liberate the people of Liore from his ideological tyranny.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.260
So, Science Rules Faith drools!

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:35.960
Right?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.160
Well, not so fast!

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.200
In the following episode the brothers are sent to study under

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.500
the Sewing-Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.300
Tucker was the first alchemist to 
successfully create a talking chimera

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.220
and tries to repeat his success in order to retain his state alchemists certification

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.960
The Elrics' fascination quickly turns to horror and in one of the biggest gut punches in anime history

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.880
We see THIS!

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.700
Yeah, that's right!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.660
Tucker actually used his family dog and his own daughter as components to create his chimera

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.820
But far from feeling remorse, Tucker claims he was only doing what science demands

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.640
In the face of such an artocity

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.400
science no longer seemed

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.820
so innocent does it?

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.980
so where does this conflict between science and Faith lead us?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.420
Tucker, the amoral alchemist in search of

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.360
scientific knowledge at any cost largely sets the tone for the rest of the show.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.220
Over at 64 episodes,

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.760
"Brotherhood" Forces us to question the value of single-mindedly clinging to science and the

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.640
consequences of reducing all knowledge to scientific terms

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.920
A mode of thought loosely known in the real world as

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.800
Now, I know what you're thinking.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.220
Jared, doubting science is what people in a cult do

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.760
But just humoring.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.340
When Philosophers critique scientism

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.900
they're not saying that science is a lie.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:12.500
What they're criticizing is how we put Scientific knowledge above all other knowledge

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.820
And how we try to reduce other forms of knowledge into it.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.540
According to Philosopher Paul Feyerabend, science is just one of many competing

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.900
explanatory frameworks one which is neither as rational nor consistent as it pretends to be.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.680
Feyerabend's favorite example is

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:33.660
Copernicus, whose heliocentric model of the Universe was actually rejected by scientists of his day.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:40.220
To them, Aristotle's idea of celestial spheres offered a fuller explanation of why the planets moved in the sky?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.160
While Copernicus's model could correctly calculate the movement of the planets,

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.240
it couldn't explain why they moved as they did until Newton's theory on Gravity was

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.080
published over a century later.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.480
Science in this case wasn't interested in the truth so much as self-preservation

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.840
Like any ideology, Feyerabend worries at an unquestioning acceptance of it

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.720
like with Liore and Leto-ism

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.700
can lead to some potentially disastrous results

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.310
In his book against method in science in a free society,

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:09.500
Feyerabend asks,

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.300
And monsters are exactly what science creates in the world of "Brotherhood"

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.500
such as man-made Chimeras that are referred to as ungodly experiments

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.900
This impersonal, dehumanizing aspect of alchemy is enshrined in

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.560
"The Law of Equivalent Exchange"

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:43.120
Which inherently reduces objects animals and even people to their physical components

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:48.960
The Elric Brothers' entire Journey starts because the two believe they can bring their mother back to life by simply

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.260
transmuting the basic ingredients of a human being

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.680
This dehumanizing nature is furthered by one of Alchemy's most sought-after creations

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.140
"The Philosopher's Stone"

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.400
When Ed and Al decode Doctor Marcoh's notes

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.160
They realize the key ingredient to the stone...

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:05.780
is human life!!!

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:18.210
The stone is the ultimate product of alchemy

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.089
allowing its users to ignore the law of equivalent exchange

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.600
But even though the stone can restore

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:29.360
Ed and Al's bodies, the two are reluctant if not just plain unwilling to use the stone.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.340
in contrast, the "Homonculi",

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:36.380
Artificial humans powered by Philosopher Stones regurgitate scientis's big philosophy.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:41.120
Reducing the souls trapped within the stones to mere alchemic principles

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:07.320
While Ed and Al both use the power of the stones on one occasion each, they do so while respecting the

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.380
autonomy of those souls.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.860
This distinguishes the brothers as moral according to Philosopher

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.700
For Kant, people are never meant to be used or reduced to calculations,

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.079
but rather are always a goal in themselves

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.340
But Ed and Al's problem with alchemy is larger than its impersonal nature

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.960
But also its subservience to the military.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.320
Alchemy is so under the control of the Amestrian government that there are actually three

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.880
state appointed tenets of Alchemy.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:00.580
The first of which,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.040
Is LITERALLY obey the military

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:14.720
In fact, State Alchemists are generally referred to as dogs of the military and even as human weapons!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.980
In his book "Science Wars",

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:26.840
sociologist Stanley Aronowitz argues that scientists often view themselves as

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.400
Yet scientists funding must come from SOMEWHERE

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.000
and often it's from corporations

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.420
or the state.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.620
As such scientists don't really own their discoveries

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.020
and have little say about their application.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.440
Throughout the anime, Ed constantly clashes with this militarization of science by the state

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.460
and his own complicity with it

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.120
as Alex Armstrong succinctly puts it...

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:09.240
We even see this military influence to store the basic

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.260
principles of science.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.080
When Ed and Al reminisce about being trained on a desert island as children,

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.580
they come to the epiphany that

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.600
Alchemy is all about understanding the natural flow of energy

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.280
both deconstructing AND reconstructing it

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.240
But this principle is later twisted in the mouths of the military.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:42.820
In justifying destroying the whole country and slaughtering its population,

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.520
one general even goes so far and to rephrase it as

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.040
"Alchemic Rebirth"

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.820
As tools of the government,

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:10.780
Alchemists have become the very instruments of the series' chief antagonist

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.140
"Father"

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.080
who controls the Amestrian state.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.680
Father desires nothing more than to assume the mantle of God.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.200
A goal which he's used

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:19.940
Alchemy,

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.240
countless military Conflicts

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:24.600
and MILLIONS of innocent lives to prepare for.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:28.180
In fact Amestris' most brutal and heartless war,

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.300
"The Ishbalan War of Exterminaton

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:33.020
was fought just to further Father's plan.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:37.340
And it's this war were the state alchemists made their largest military impact

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.660
What's shocking about Ishbal isn't just the devastating force

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.840
that Alchemy wrecked on it

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.760
But the scientific language used to explain it.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.800
Even the good guys here can't help but couch what's essentially

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.640
GENOCIDE in these sterile scientific terms

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.860
In fact, this sanitizing nature of scientific language is what

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.379
escalated the Ishbalan war war to new heights

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:17.590
As Führer King Bradley told the high priest of Ishbala when he offered himself up in exchange for a ceasefire,

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:20.180
"The Law of Equivalent Exchange" won't allow it

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.420
Hell, the fuhrer even considers his wife to be nothing more than an

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.540
expendable pawn for his greater scheme.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:41.040
Now, if the title of "Führer" is raising eyebrows among you,

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.300
there's a good reason for that.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.920
the country Amestris is reminiscent of pre-World War 2 Germany.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.040
A militant nation expanding beyond its borders and a blond-haired blue-eyed

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:52.520
army, whose uniforms look a lot like that of the SS.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.240
Even the "Might is Right" motivation behind Nazi Germany,

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.140
bubbles to the surface in Amestris.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.700
As General Raven invokes Social Darwinism

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.120
to justify mass extermination.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:15.960
And if that's not enough to convince you then you only have to compare Amestris' human experiment to that of

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.040
Auschwitz' lead doctor,

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.600
Dr. Josef Mengele

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.720
Whether it's raising babies in underground laboratories,

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.520
stitching together people and animals

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.100
or ripping souls from bodies

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.800
It's hard to say that Amestris lacks the same want and cruelty

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.780
and morbid scientific curiosity

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.770
that defined Mengele's operations

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:37.879
Mengele established a kindergarten at Auschwitz for his younger experiment

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:41.100
Allegedly stitching two gypsy girls together.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.579
And if he could have Gotten his hands on a literal soul,

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:45.710
he probably would have mutilated it

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:46.730
Oh, yeah

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.960
Did we mention that Feyerabend actually fought

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.840
as a Lieutenant in World War 2?

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:53.119
Even earning an iron cross in the process?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.980
Witnessing firsthand the Scientific arguments

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.160
made by a dictatorship for war and genocide,

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.900
it's no surprise that Feyeraben

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:01.980
would one day propose

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.360
a separation between science and state

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:07.000
with ultimate power resting in Democracy

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.060
In his lecture,

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:10.780
he argued,

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.180
So it's safe to say that "Fullmetal Alchemist"

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:32.000
presents a cautionary tale about the blind adherence to science

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.960
But what does it say about Faith?

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.300
Well throughout its 64 episode run,

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.680
Faith is often portrayed as another explanatory model

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:41.940
Another source of truth and power.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.520
In fact for a show populated almost entirely by scientists,

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.340
the characters make a number of appeals to Faith.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.720
In the episode "The Miracle of Rush Valley" (Episode 11)

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.560
Ed an Al witness the delivery of a baby

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.980
become awestruck

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.120
and point out the limitations of Alchemy

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.420
Dr.. Marcoh the alchemist largely responsible

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.100
for the creation of the Philosopher's stone

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:12.440
during the Ishbal Civil war calls it fate that he met the

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:16.460
Ishbalan, Scar, before the two set out together to challenge the government.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:20.340
Similarly Knox ,who worked as a doctor during the war and was subsequently

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:24.380
estranged from his family invokes God when they returned to him.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:33.380
Even Bradley, a homunculus, wonders if his own death at

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:35.540
the hand of Scar was providence.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:47.260
Bradley who mercilessly killed the Ishbalan people during the war

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:49.850
was told that God would strike him down one day

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:54.529
And it was the sun looking like a crescent moon which together symbolized

00:14:54.529 --> 00:14:59.180
God in alchemy that blinded him and allowed scar to strike the finishing blow

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.420
So is that the thematic takeaway of the show?

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.300
Science is bad Faith is good.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.320
So keep on praying?

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.120
Well, not quite

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:09.480
See the problem with scientism

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:12.700
Isn't that science is bad and that non science is good.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:16.139
Feyarabend isn't giving the middle finger to vaccines and posting about

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.520
chemtrails on Twitter.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:22.180
Nope, instead his main contention is that,

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.760
What Feyarabend opposes is any unreflective veneration of any ideology.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.400
Because it inhibits free thought

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:36.020
As it turns out, the blind following of science as the arbiter of truth,

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.980
is just as harmful as the blind following of

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.980
Faith as the arbiter of truth.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.520
Whether its Father Cornello or the "Homonculi"

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.080
using the Leto-ists is to incite violence against their enemies,

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:50.900
or scar using his God, "Ishvala" to justify his vengeance against the alchemists

00:15:56.080 --> 00:16:00.120
Faith alone can be every bit just as scary as science

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.849
Characters grow in "Brotherhood" when they realized the limitations of adhering to any one ideology

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:10.739
Edward and Alphonse for example begin to question the foundations of Western Alchemy which

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.200
Supposedly takes its energy from the tectonic movements of the Earth's Mantle

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.260
when Father manages to cancel it out

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:19.920
It's their quest for an explanation that leads them to science's

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:23.720
eastern equivalent, Alkahestry, which uses life energy from the planet

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:25.760
It's ultimately bridging the gap

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.160
between these two ideologies

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.660
that allows our heroes to eventually triumph

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:33.460
The two different scientists come together to make a reverse transmutation circle

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:35.800
that saves the lives of all Amestris

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.860
Perhaps no character embodies

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.100
its development more than Scar.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.360
A survivor of the is fallen war of extinction

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.100
Scar targets State Alchemists out of revenge.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.760
To him not only are alchemists weapons

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.080
but they transgress against God

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.290
who alone possesses the right to create

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.840
But as Scar learns more about Amestris,

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.680
he realizes how wrong he was to seek vengeance

00:17:04.069 --> 00:17:07.280
Scar who once cloaked his actions in the words of God,

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:10.659
finally understands that no ideology can justify murder

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.180
Scar even breaks from the strict laws that govern his fate.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.720
Making use of the very alchemy that his God abhors

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.460
in order to save the country he once hated

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:32.440
Scar's transformation stands in stark contrast to the show's main antagonist

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:33.220
"Father"

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:36.400
who clings to his single-Minded belief in science

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.480
Father becomes obsessed with the power of alchemy

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:42.100
and takes this obsession to the logical extreme

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.540
viewing mankind is little more than materials

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:49.060
for him to use in becoming God

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.220
Blinded by scientism,

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.000
Father can't understand the value of human emotions

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.680
and discards them in his attempt to become perfect

00:17:56.940 --> 00:18:00.260
he literally rips the seven deadly sins from himself

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:00.980
Lust

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:01.640
Greed

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:02.360
Sloth

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.320
Gluttony

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.040
Envy

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:04.740
Wrath

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:05.580
and Pride

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:07.520
who in turn become the other "Homunculi"

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.493
Ultimately, it's this conviction in the absolute supremacy of science

00:18:11.493 --> 00:18:12.840
and the ability to achieve

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:16.040
perfection through it that undoes "Father"

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.040
the souls trapped in the Philosopher's stone

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.540
which he dismissed as mere energy,

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.160
begin to assert their will

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.740
and repel against him

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.860
Father's conception of a soul as a mere

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.500
ingredient fails to account for the autonomy of these individuals

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.280
After an epic punch to the gut,

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:34.477
Father is finally killed and dragged back into the void

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.580
from whence he came

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.240
where he meets the real God

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:38.900
a being called "Truth".

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.360
Still desperately clinging to scientism

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:43.420
Father demands to know what he did wrong

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.680
But unlike Scar and others,

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:57.840
Father refused to recognize any kind of human wisdom beyond alchemy.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:10.200
All of this goes to show what makes Ed and Al particularly

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.620
special throughout the series

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:14.660
They're humble rejection of a single ideology.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:15.689
From the show's outset,

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.940
the two grapple with what alchemy is

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.000
and what it means to be a State Alchemist.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:28.400
It's this questioning that makes the brothers seen both naive and likable

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:32.500
At the brothers core is a strong desire to discover their own truth

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:35.520
When psychopath extraordinaire "Solf J. Kimblee"

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.780
has Alphonse cornered

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.140
he wonders why our hero doesn't just take the Philosopher's stone

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.340
and get his body back

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:49.040
Sure the country would face certain destruction from "Father"

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:51.820
But that's just equivalent exchange in action

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:55.380
In order to get their bodies back. They have to give up the world's safety

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.200
But Al rejects that alchemic worldview

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.860
reaffirming their desire to find their OWN truth

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:11.940
It's this search for possibilities that distinguishes the brothers

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.040
and allows Ed to make his final transmutation

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:18.380
After Al sacrifices himself in order to give Ed his arm back

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:21.220
Ed follows his brother into the portal to bring him back.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.640
When asked by the truth what price he'll pay,

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:26.940
Ed smiles and offers his ability to perform alchemy

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.840
and recognizes the arrogance

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.840
in thinking that alchemy could explain everything

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:32.800
let alone solve all his problems.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:43.480
Unlike father who couldn't accept his place in the universe

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:46.500
and equated Alchemy with power Ed knows the truth,

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.940
With their bodies back in the day saved,

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.680
what's left for our heroes to do?

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.369
in typical Elric fashion,

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.420
it's to keep searching for truth

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.060
and new methods to discover it

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.260
as Alphonse puts it

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:12.640
they want to give back

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.560
to the people who helped them all along their journey

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:16.960
But it's not a simple give and take

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.060
not a cold formula like the "Law of Equivalent Exchange"

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:34.800
To that end, Al is travelling east

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:35.840
and Ed, west

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:38.120
In hopes of gathering all knowledge

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:40.060
to make this principle a reality

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:43.060
Of course old habits tend to die hard

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.240
and when Ed finally confesses his feelings to Winry.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.740
it comes out like this

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:58.380
Of course, maybe Ed didn't need to go so far from home

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:01.840
to realize that science alone can't explain everything

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:11.940
We waited 64 episodes for that moment, and it was damn worth it

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.420
So what do you think Wisecrack?

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:16.479
Will pure devotion to science lead us on a dark path?

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:18.680
Do we need to inject a little,

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:19.700
I don't know, maybe

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.920
philosophy into how we look at the world?

